   "widgets_values": [
    "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the source video for the target video edit.\n<Picture 1> is a product photo of the yellow metal thermos; only the thermos is used and its plain white background is discarded.\n<Subject 1> is the yellow metal thermos from <Picture 1>: a tall straight cylindrical insulated bottle with a matte lemon-yellow powder-coated body, rounded shoulders, a short flat matte yellow screw cap, and one narrow brushed-steel band between the cap and the shoulder, no label and no text.\n<Subject 2> is the man in <Video 1>: short dark hair, a trimmed dark beard, a black ribbed knitted crew-neck sweater, looking down at the object held in both hands.\n<Subject 3> is the setting in <Video 1>: a warmly lit modern kitchen at night, wood panels, lit shelves with glassware, softly out of focus behind him.\n<Subject 4> is the red wine bottle held in the man's hands in <Video 1>: a dark glass bottle with a dark-red capsule and a cream paper label.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + reference generation] The target video is an edited version of <Video 1>. It keeps the same two shots, the same hard cut, the same framing and the same slow motion of <Subject 2>, but the object in his hands is <Subject 1>, the yellow thermos of <Picture 1>, in every frame of both shots, held in exactly the same place, at the same angle and in the same grip as the bottle was. There is no wine bottle anywhere in the target video.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (source video editing): fully_preserved - the two shots, the hard cut at 00:01.708, the framing and subject scale of each shot, the man's slow head and hand movement, the kitchen background and the light are copied frame for frame.\n<Picture 1> (object reference): fully_preserved - the shape, colour, cap and steel band of the thermos are used; its white background is discarded.\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - matte yellow body, rounded shoulders, flat yellow cap and one brushed-steel band.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - identity, face, beard, hair, hands, fingers and the black knitted sweater are retained.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - the kitchen, shelves, glassware and warm light are retained.\n<Subject 4> (replaced in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): removed - the wine bottle, its dark glass, red capsule and paper label do not appear in any frame; <Subject 1> is held in its place.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a clean, sharp, warmly lit interior portrait in natural colour with shallow depth of field. No text and no lettering anywhere.\n[Shot 1] From 00:00.000 to 00:01.708, exactly as in the first shot of <Video 1>, a vertical waist-up view: <Subject 2> stands centred with his head near the top of the frame, looking down, while both hands hold <Subject 1> diagonally across his chest with the flat yellow cap pointing up and to the left of the frame. His fingers wrap around the matte yellow body, and he turns the thermos slowly, just as in <Video 1>. Behind him <Subject 3> stays softly out of focus.\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.708 a hard cut, exactly as in <Video 1>, to a closer vertical view of <Subject 2>: his head and shoulders fill the upper half of the frame, and both hands hold <Subject 1> diagonally in the lower left with the flat yellow cap and the narrow brushed-steel band near the left edge. He looks down at it and turns it slowly until 00:03.042, just as in <Video 1>. <Subject 3> stays softly out of focus behind him.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSilence. No dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
